<DocsLayout
  title="Getting Started"
  description="Start using Axon Editor with a workspace, files, terminal, and settings."
>
  <h1>Getting Started</h1>

  <p>
    Axon is a desktop code editor built around real workspace behavior: open a
    folder, edit files, use panes, run terminals, inspect Git changes, and tune
    the editor from settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Recommended first flow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Install the build that matches your platform from the download page.</li>
    <li>Open a folder as your workspace.</li>
    <li>Create or open a file from the sidebar.</li>
    <li>Open the terminal and run your project commands.</li>
    <li>Open settings to choose a theme, font preset, and language-server options.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Important notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>macOS builds are unsigned personal builds until signing is available.</li>
    <li>Some language servers still need system runtimes such as a JDK or .NET.</li>
    <li>Python projects can use a selected virtual environment for imports.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Continue with <a href="/docs/getting-started/installation">Installation</a>
    or open the <a href="/docs/getting-started/first-project">First Project</a>
    guide.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
